  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients except sulfur, yeast extract, vitamins and sulfide."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Adjust pH to 3.5 with H2SO4 and sparge medium with 100% CO2 gas for 30 – 45 min to make it anoxic."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials containing the appropriate amount of sulfur."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Heat vessels containing medium to 90°C for 1 hour on each of 3 succesive days."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Add yeast extract, vitamins (sterilized by filtration) and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "The sulfide stock solution (3% w/v) should be neutralized before use (see medium 29)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "The pH of the complete medium should be at 3.5 - 3.8."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "For DSM 16705 reduce the amount of yeast extract to 0.10 g/l and supplement medium after sterilization with 2.00 g/l D-glucose added from a sterile anoxic stock solution."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "First dissolve FeCl2 in the HCl, then dilute in water, add and dissolve the other salts. Finally make up to 1000.0 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}